    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "When to invoke",
      "prov:value": "That is the cheapest collision to\n  find, because it is the one found BEFORE either of you has written\n  anything. Owner, same day: *\"potential collision by looking at\n  beans = coordinate\"*. How to read a sibling's state out of the\n  store, and the boundary of that inference, is\n  [`bean-coordination`](../../../work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md) §\"Where a sibling\n  session is visible from\" — not restated here."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "When to invoke",
      "prov:value": "How to read a sibling's state out of the\n  store, and the boundary of that inference, is\n  [`bean-coordination`](../../../work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md) §\"Where a sibling\n  session is visible from\" — not restated here.\n- **When you START any new unit of work — before the first edit.** A\n  new story, epic, feature or task bean, an issue, CRDM Phase 6, a\n  workplan tranche, or a handover pickup runs the collision review in\n  §\"Starting new work\" below, scaled to its blast radius, and records\n  it in the workplan bean. Owner, 2026-10-02 (#1885).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1885",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Watching for sibling-PR contradictions",
      "prov:value": "## What actually reaches a sibling — measured, 2026-09-21",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What actually reaches a sibling — measured, 2026-09-21",
      "prov:value": "### Since 2026-10: a spawned helper is reachable, and the owner's authority is not relayed\n\nThe table above predates the remote-session tools. A session that has\n`create_session` and `send_message` (the `claude-code-remote` server) **can**\nseed a helper session and message a cloud session it lists: both worked from\nthe drain coordinator on 2026-10-10 and 2026-10-20 (epic `ml9h`).\nReaching it does not give it the owner's authority (bean `yex5`).\n\nWhat lane B of that drain hit: its permission layer refused a push, a\n`send_message` back, and finally a read-only `beans show`, because its task\narrived from another session rather than from the owner. It also refused to\ntreat the coordinator's relayed \"4 h merge window\" as the owner's ruling. That refusal was\ncorrect.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ml9h",
        "bean yex5",
        "2026-10-10",
        "2026-10-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-10",
        "2026-10-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Eleven sessions is the normal case, not the exception",
      "prov:value": "The same measurement: eleven sessions on `litlfred/folio-assistant`,\neach on its own branch, each merging `main` on a loop. One branch took\n**four** base merges in three hours, three of them conflicted. Main\nmoved 109, 38, 20, 24 and 28 commits between them.\n\nA session that treats a conflict as an accident will treat all four as\naccidents. The rate IS the environment, and the thing to do about it\nis coordinate earlier, not merge harder."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Crossing into a sibling's subject — permitted, and what it costs",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-22, on stream 3 of the #956 consolidation rewriting the `yg29`\nmilestone it had been told not to touch:\n\n> *\"crossing stream is ok, but /coordinate and be aware of potential collisions.\n> try avoid duplicating work.\"*\n\nTwo rulings, and they are not the same one twice.\n\n**1. The stream that owns a milestone's WORK may repair the milestone.**\n`check-stale-paths.ts` reserved that repair to \"the bean's OWNER\" on the ground\nthat *\"a milestone is a statement of what its owner believes the goal needs\nnext, and rewriting somebody else's belief is not a checker's to do.\"* That\nground still holds **for a checker** — a gate that guesses replaces a stale\nbelief with an invented one. It does **not** hold for a session that has\nre-measured the goal's whole surface. Stream 3 repaired `yg29` and found two\ndefects a path detector structurally cannot see: `hqku` carried as a live\n\"blocked on the owner\" for two days after it completed, and *\"the IRIS replica has no\n`docs/`\"* against a directory holding three rendered pages.\n\nSo the line is **checker vs. session**, not owner vs. non-owner. A session\nrepairing somebody's milestone re-measures every line it rewrites, in a fresh\ncontainer, by running the thing — and says which clause it could not verify.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean yg29",
        "bean hqku",
        "#956",
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "The collision surface is FILES, and it is predictable before you touch one",
      "prov:value": "It does not find two\nsessions about to edit the same *file* from different subjects, which is how\nthe #956 consolidation nearly lost a baseline:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#956"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The collision surface is FILES, and it is predictable before you touch one",
      "prov:value": "| a shared bean like `k59d` | every stream appends its own outcome. **\"An append cannot collide\" is false when two sessions append**, because both land at EOF. That precedent is recorded in `k59d` itself and is wrong as stated. |\n| generated dirs (`auto-docs/`, `skill-instructions/`, kg-qa sidecars) | nobody edits them, everybody regenerates them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean k59d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Duplicated work is measured in what was already pushed, not in what is open",
      "prov:value": "The same consolidation measured `p5wm`'s critical path **twice** — once in the\nsession writing the stream claims, once in the stream that received them,\nreaching the identical answer (five live steps, not eight). Neither was wrong\nand both were competent; the second was free to skip. Before re-deriving a\nmeasurement",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean p5wm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Starting new work — a collision review, recorded before the first edit (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "<a id=\"before-a-platform-refactor\"></a>\nFormerly §\"Before a platform refactor\". The rule began there and now covers\nthe start of any unit of SDLC work; citations of the old title land here.\n\nOwner, 2026-10-02, on issue #1885, verbatim:\n\n> *\"(in genreal update agent-agent coorindation/hadover skills - if you are\n> working on a refactor of the platform, review active agents/beans for impact\n> and coordiante)\"*\n\nOwner, 2026-10-02, later the same day, verbatim:\n\n> *\"Before any platform refactor, a session must now review the open PR-->\n> genrealizes to parts of the SDLC / begining on a new story/epic or so...\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1885",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The five steps, in order, before any file is edited",
      "prov:value": "### Worked example — #1885, bean `gp2f`\n\nThis is the full-depth case: a platform refactor, with overlaps found and\nowners messaged.\n\nThe refactor moves the per-page nav, the harness bar, icons, scripts and the\nIG chrome CSS into shared cached assets. It touches the layout of every page\non the site. Before any edit, the review found active sibling work on **every\nlayout file the plan needed**:\n\n| sibling | its PRs | shared files | `gp2f` phases affected |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| navbar session (bean `ob3m`) | #1804, #1805, #1808, #1819 | `docs-ui.css`, `docs-ui.js`, `_includes/generated/navbar-footer.html`, `harness_details.html`, `head_custom.html`, `harness-tiles.md` | B, C, D, E |\n| fhir-ast session (bean `wnhh`) | #1816 | the FHIR IG layer's `scripts/gen-ig-pages.ts` | A |\n| the trust IG IG session | #1766 | the `gen-ig-pages` area | A |\n\nIf the review had been skipped, five PRs would have been rebased into a\nrefactor of the files they were editing.\n\nWhat happened instead:\n\n- The review went into `gp2f` before any edit.\n- The three owning sessions were messaged with the plan and asked for an order.\n- The only work that started was work that touches none of their files: this\n  section, and a read-only baseline measurement of page sizes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean gp2f",
        "bean ob3m",
        "bean wnhh",
        "#1885",
        "#1804",
        "#1805",
        "#1808",
        "#1819",
        "#1816",
        "#1766"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/coordinate.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A spawned helper is reachable, and the owner's authority is not relayed",
      "prov:value": "Item 5 added 2026-11-05 (bean `55ka`), after helpers spawned by\n`session_01VQDpPffYARDQ8juksAZScf` (`k3vv`) and\n`session_01VQDpPfGantMCt7AV4LCCK2` (`drnh`) asked the owner in prose without\ncards when `add_repo` was refused or a scope decision arose. Owner, 2026-11-05:\n*\"did you and your siblings forget I am disabled? why has it not been heeded\nlately?\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 55ka",
        "2026-11-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-05"
      ]
    }
  ]
